        "date": "2026-11-09T01:16:24Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(setup): per-setup stock source and the incoming stock on the setup page\n\nA setup after the first picks where its stock comes from: \"Its own stock\n(the Stock node)\" or \"What <previous setup> leaves behind\" (the machined\nbody #317 carries). Stored on SetupDef as Option<StockSource>; unpicked\nreads #317's implicit rule (linked or held differently: what the previous\nsetup leaves; same hold unlinked: its own stock, the M3.2 A clip), so\nevery existing document simulates, posts and stamps unchanged.\n\n- SetSetupStockSource: undoable, validated at construction (not the first\n  setup, a carry the sim can verify, a real change); the pick rides the\n  setup's operation stamps, so its operations go Stale.\n- Sim: FromPrevious carries; Own keeps the clip in the same hold and\n  takes a new block in a different hold. The gouges of a block left\n  behind fold into the program verdict, never dropped.\n- Setup page: the option enabled from the second setup on; a refused\n  carry disables it with the reason; the incoming body's box and volume\n  are shown, measured once per document version.\n- Setup sheet: STOCK states the source and the incoming box/volume.\n- Project v57: \"stock_source\": \"own\" | \"from_previous\"; absent is\n  unpicked; an unknown word is corrupt.\n\nDecisions: docs/decisions/320-stock-source.md. Viewport preview: #406.\n\nFixes #320\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
